  "notes": "Captured full-page screenshot is almost entirely black: the tall 1440x3446 capture window tripped the app's orientation guard, which renders a red monospace 'SYSTEM HALT / DISPLAY_OUTPUT_INVALID / ERROR_CODE: PORTRAIT_MODE_DETECTED' overlay. The interface was coded from the real 900px first viewport and the live page. Dock box uses DOM coordinates from the tall layout, where it was re-centred at y≈1505; at 900px it sits at y≈232–667. The site is a macOS-like web desktop: translucent plum (#332038) windows with red/yellow/green traffic lights and backdrop blur, a magenta (#d453f6) accent on folder icons, the active path chip, item counts and badges, an aurora-borealis-over-rocky-shore photo wallpaper, and a left vertical dock of rounded-square app tiles (blue-gradient Finder/Browser/Mail) with dot indicators under running apps. Content is a narrative security/CTF scenario (student Mira's mail and documents). Filed new-entry proposal 'windowed-desktop' for the overlapping-windows desktop metaphor, and new value empty-state cause 'no-selection'."
